      "message": "Done! I've fixed the accent handling in the `slugify` function. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n**The Problem:**\nThe original code had a `elif ch.isalpha(): continue` block that skipped non-ASCII alphabetic characters (like accented letters). So \"Café\" became \"caf\" instead of \"cafe\".\n\n**The Solution:**\nI added Unicode normalization using `unicodedata.normalize(\"NFD\", ...)` which decomposes accented characters into their base letter plus combining marks. Then I filter out the combining marks (Unicode category \"Mn\") to leave just ASCII letters.\n\n**Verification:**\n- ✅ All existing tests pass (\"hello-world\", \"abc\")\n- ✅ Accented characters now convert properly (\"Café\" → \"cafe\", \"Pöstälödé\" → \"postalode-world\")\n- ✅ Spaces still convert to dashes correctly",
